Catfall is a monk technique that enables graceful recovery from falls that
would injure or kill lesser individuals. Through training in body awareness
and aerial maneuvering, monks learn to twist and position themselves during
a fall to minimize or eliminate impact damage.

This passive skill activates automatically when falling. A successful
Catfall allows the monk to land gracefully on their feet, taking no damage
and maintaining their standing position. Failed attempts result in a normal
hard landing.

The technique requires split-second adjustments and complete body control.
Masters of Catfall can survive drops that would be fatal to others, making
monks surprisingly difficult to kill through environmental hazards.

